00:51:32.200 --> 00:51:36.400
But John and I were actually listening to an Interpol song.

1248
00:51:37.000 --> 00:51:37.780
Which song?

1249
00:51:37.820 --> 00:51:38.600
I don't remember.

1250
00:51:38.600 --> 00:51:40.020
But you know it was Interpol.

1251
00:51:40.180 --> 00:51:40.460
Yes.

1252
00:51:40.640 --> 00:51:41.600
I remember that.

1253
00:51:41.740 --> 00:51:50.440
And I think, I think that was John's actual iPod and that he suggested that song, that we listened to the song.

1254
00:51:50.740 --> 00:51:52.920
Aw, jam fans are going to love that.

1255
00:51:53.020 --> 00:51:53.220
Yeah.

1256
00:51:53.340 --> 00:51:54.820
And that was also lovely.

1257
00:51:54.960 --> 00:51:56.560
Same warm summer evening.

1258
00:51:56.760 --> 00:51:57.720
It was awesome.

1259
00:51:57.900 --> 00:52:04.460
So we talked to Melora a little bit about the next scene, which is Michael and Jan in the parking lot.

1260
00:52:04.640 --> 00:52:06.700
That's at 15 minutes, 21 seconds.

1261
00:52:06.700 --> 00:52:08.380
It is the big smooch.

1262
00:52:08.540 --> 00:52:09.680
Yes, the big smooch.

1263
00:52:09.800 --> 00:52:10.060
All right.

1264
00:52:10.180 --> 00:52:16.640
So I feel like there's just this brilliant moment, and I don't know if it was written or if Steve improvised this,

1265
00:52:16.760 --> 00:52:25.200
that just shows how over the moon giddy Michael is that him and Jan just kissed and that she said, let's get out of here.

1266
00:52:25.320 --> 00:52:26.240
He's so giddy.

1267
00:52:26.320 --> 00:52:29.220
And I wrote down the scene because I thought it was so adorable.

1268
00:52:29.440 --> 00:52:31.320
It's at 15 minutes, 21 seconds.

1269
00:52:31.800 --> 00:52:35.280
Jan says, Jan is sort of like all of a sudden camera aware, right?

1270
00:52:35.420 --> 00:52:35.600
Yeah.

1271
00:52:35.600 --> 00:52:37.260
She's looking for the camera.

1272
00:52:37.360 --> 00:52:38.360
Is this getting caught on tape?

1273
00:52:38.440 --> 00:52:38.560
Yeah.

1274
00:52:38.580 --> 00:52:40.440
She doesn't find the camera, but she wonders.

1275
00:52:40.720 --> 00:52:40.920
Right.

1276
00:52:41.060 --> 00:52:42.240
And so she says, let's go.

1277
00:52:42.360 --> 00:52:43.200
And Michael goes, what?

1278
00:52:43.340 --> 00:52:44.340
And she goes, let's go.

1279
00:52:44.460 --> 00:52:46.100
And he says, where are we going?

1280
00:52:46.240 --> 00:52:46.720
Oh, OK.

1281
00:52:46.880 --> 00:52:47.480
Doesn't matter.

1282
00:52:47.780 --> 00:52:48.640
Going to the go-go.

1283
00:52:49.060 --> 00:52:50.380
Going to the go-go.

1284
00:52:50.800 --> 00:52:53.940
That was so cute.

1285
00:52:53.940 --> 00:52:55.780
He's just so excited.

1286
00:52:56.220 --> 00:52:57.280
I thought it was adorable.

1287
00:52:57.580 --> 00:52:57.880
All right.

1288
00:52:57.980 --> 00:52:59.560
So it's the next morning now.

1289
00:52:59.760 --> 00:53:02.280
The Dunder Mifflin film crew enters the office.

1290
00:53:02.440 --> 00:53:03.120
Do they have a key?

1291
00:53:03.620 --> 00:53:04.420
Do you notice that?

1292
00:53:07.500 --> 00:53:08.240
I know.

1293
00:53:08.460 --> 00:53:10.260
Maybe he never locked the door that night.

1294
00:53:10.280 --> 00:53:18.180
Why is Dwight in blue underwear on his tank top under like a foil, like a FEMA foil blanket?

1295
00:53:18.360 --> 00:53:22.960
Well, I'll tell you, there was a very big meeting about what underwear he would wear.

1296
00:53:23.100 --> 00:53:23.960
Of course there was.

1297
00:53:24.020 --> 00:53:24.320
Yes.

1298
00:53:24.560 --> 00:53:25.460
Would it be boxers?

1299
00:53:25.540 --> 00:53:26.460
Would it be briefs?

1300
00:53:26.560 --> 00:53:27.240
What color?

1301
00:53:27.440 --> 00:53:28.620
This is what they decided.

1302
00:53:28.840 --> 00:53:31.120
Of course there's a huge meeting about Dwight's underwear.

1303
00:53:31.280 --> 00:53:31.960
Of course.

1304
00:53:32.160 --> 00:53:32.360
Yeah.

1305
00:53:32.660 --> 00:53:33.320
I know.

1306
00:53:33.320 --> 00:53:36.800
And they decided on those blue, kind of like tighty-whities.

1307
00:53:37.360 --> 00:53:37.900
Yeah.

1308
00:53:38.280 --> 00:53:40.620
They're, I guess, very slouchy.

1309
00:53:40.700 --> 00:53:41.400
Very baggy.

1310
00:53:41.760 --> 00:53:43.840
Oh, you know Rain loved that.

1311
00:53:43.960 --> 00:53:45.060
He loved every second.

1312
00:53:46.100 --> 00:53:48.820
What about the scene where he runs to the window?

1313
00:53:49.020 --> 00:53:50.460
Angela sees Jan.

1314
00:53:50.740 --> 00:53:51.260
That's right.

1315
00:53:51.420 --> 00:53:54.780
So obviously the camera crew busts Jan, right?

1316
00:53:55.000 --> 00:53:55.120
Yeah.

1317
00:53:55.140 --> 00:53:55.940
She's so busted.

1318
00:53:55.940 --> 00:53:59.960
But there are two Dunder Mifflin employees who also now know.

1319
00:53:59.960 --> 00:54:05.580
Angela, who's arrived early in the parking lot, and Dwight, who's peeping down from the window.

1320
00:54:06.140 --> 00:54:07.800
And Jan sees Dwight.

1321
00:54:07.940 --> 00:54:10.340
I'm assuming she sees Angela as she drives by.

1322
00:54:10.480 --> 00:54:12.360
But I love that Dwight and Angela.

1323
00:54:12.360 --> 00:54:13.680
Oh, I think she totally clocks you.

1324
00:54:13.800 --> 00:54:14.160
Oh, yeah.

1325
00:54:14.300 --> 00:54:15.160
I do too.

1326
00:54:15.160 --> 00:54:20.420
But I love that Dwight and Angela, who go on to have their secret relationship, totally bust Jan.

1327
00:54:21.620 --> 00:54:31.940
I love that it's Angela in the parking lot because I feel like the very last person who you want to see during your walk of shame is Angela.

1328
00:54:33.020 --> 00:54:33.680
Exactly.

1329
00:54:34.580 --> 00:54:34.860
All right.

1330
00:54:35.060 --> 00:54:40.160
So Michael arrives into the office with his delicious secret.

1331
00:54:40.480 --> 00:54:41.560
He's so giddy.

1332
00:54:41.560 --> 00:54:48.040
I felt like Melora described that so well, how sweet and innocent and happy he is that he –

1333
00:54:48.040 --> 00:54:50.140
Oh, he's so excited.

1334
00:54:50.460 --> 00:54:50.880
So good.

1335
00:54:50.900 --> 00:54:53.640
And he really is like, I'm not going to talk about it, right?

1336
00:54:53.680 --> 00:54:54.820
No, I'm not going to speak about it.

1337
00:54:54.860 --> 00:54:56.540
He's like, gentlemen, don't kiss and tell, and neither do I.

1338
00:54:56.660 --> 00:54:57.080
Ha, ha, ha.

1339
00:54:57.260 --> 00:55:00.720
You know, and then the next thing we know, he's like, we'll have to disclose.

1340
00:55:00.720 --> 00:55:01.900
We'll have to write a letter.

1341
00:55:02.060 --> 00:55:02.380
Yeah.

1342
00:55:02.700 --> 00:55:03.300
That's so true.

1343
00:55:03.460 --> 00:55:04.440
About our relationship.

1344
00:55:04.440 --> 00:55:05.800
He just – oh, man.

1345
00:55:06.020 --> 00:55:09.120
In that talking head, I love the camera work in that.

1346
00:55:09.120 --> 00:55:17.380
It's a very, very slow push-in on Michael's face, and you can just feel the camera putting

1347
00:55:17.380 --> 00:55:19.420
all this pressure on Michael to tell the truth.

1348
00:55:19.640 --> 00:55:21.000
How long does he last?

1349
00:55:21.180 --> 00:55:23.260
He lasts like 14 seconds.

1350
00:55:24.360 --> 00:55:24.800
Seconds.

1351
00:55:24.900 --> 00:55:26.620
He's like, all right, fine.

1352
00:55:26.740 --> 00:55:28.160
We went back and we –

1353
00:55:28.160 --> 00:55:28.700
To her hotel.

1354
00:55:28.840 --> 00:55:29.220
Yeah, we –

1355
00:55:29.220 --> 00:55:30.260
Made out for a little bit.

1356
00:55:30.280 --> 00:55:30.460
Made out a little.

1357
00:55:30.680 --> 00:55:32.700
I held her and she talked to me about her divorce.

1358
00:55:33.060 --> 00:55:34.000
Oh, my gosh.

1359
00:55:34.300 --> 00:55:38.280
That phone call with Jan where he goes under the desk, Greg directed that.

1360
00:55:38.280 --> 00:55:43.540
Greg told Steve, why don't you take this phone call under the desk to avoid the camera

1361
00:55:43.540 --> 00:55:43.880
crew?

1362
00:55:44.060 --> 00:55:50.020
And he said it was great because they were able to edit together all of Steve's improvisations

1363
00:55:50.020 --> 00:55:52.100
because you can't see his mouth.

1364
00:55:52.400 --> 00:55:53.820
Oh, so smart.

1365
00:55:54.020 --> 00:55:58.360
Yeah, because Steve was improvising a lot of that phone call and the things that, you know,

1366
00:55:58.420 --> 00:55:59.600
he was saying back to Jan.

1367
00:56:00.500 --> 00:56:04.960
Then we have Jim and Pam's – whoo – kind of their first fight.

1368
00:56:05.440 --> 00:56:06.040
I don't know.

1369
00:56:06.040 --> 00:56:09.660
They have that – they have that hiccup at the dojo, but this is different.

1370
00:56:09.880 --> 00:56:11.060
They have little moments.

1371
00:56:11.280 --> 00:56:14.920
I mean, he got his feelings really hurt when you suggested he try – you know, go for

1372
00:56:14.920 --> 00:56:16.240
that job at the other branch.

1373
00:56:16.420 --> 00:56:16.580
Yeah.

1374
00:56:16.880 --> 00:56:19.160
And then there was the dojo and now there's this.

1375
00:56:20.080 --> 00:56:23.440
Well, this one doesn't get resolved at the end of this episode.

1376
00:56:24.040 --> 00:56:28.580
Jim suggests to Pam that maybe they had their first date, that you could say this was their

1377
00:56:28.580 --> 00:56:29.000
first date.

1378
00:56:29.040 --> 00:56:30.160
And I want to say something.

1379
00:56:30.160 --> 00:56:34.220
I understand why Pam bristles at this.

1380
00:56:34.460 --> 00:56:36.120
Well, let me just take a minute.

1381
00:56:36.400 --> 00:56:42.240
First of all, Pam lies to Roy, boldface lies to Roy and says, I have to stay at work.

1382
00:56:42.380 --> 00:56:44.260
And he's like, are you kidding me right now?

1383
00:56:44.320 --> 00:56:45.880
And she's like, no, I have to work.

1384
00:56:45.880 --> 00:56:53.040
So, already, like, she has probably, within her moral compass, stepped over a line.

1385
00:56:53.160 --> 00:56:58.440
I think for Jim – now, look, guys, I'm a huge Jim and Pam fan, and I wanted them together

1386
00:56:58.440 --> 00:56:59.160
from the beginning.

1387
00:56:59.400 --> 00:57:03.300
But I would think, as a guy – like, I was talking to my husband about this, and he goes,

1388
00:57:03.460 --> 00:57:06.480
this is kind of a d*** move what Jim's doing.

1389
00:57:06.680 --> 00:57:08.720
You know, he knows she has a fiancé.

1390
00:57:08.720 --> 00:57:13.220
But he makes a grilled cheese sandwich, takes her up on the roof.

1391
00:57:13.380 --> 00:57:14.340
Like, he knows.

1392
00:57:14.420 --> 00:57:14.860
He knows.

1393
00:57:14.960 --> 00:57:15.720
This is his moment.

1394
00:57:15.880 --> 00:57:16.960
He's going for it.

1395
00:57:17.760 --> 00:57:20.040
Ultimately, they end up together, so it's great.

1396
00:57:20.240 --> 00:57:24.640
But that's not – that kind of breaks guy code of what you do with someone else's fiancé.

1397
00:57:25.140 --> 00:57:31.080
Well, and then I think for him to call it out so clearly out in the open, I think Pam

1398
00:57:31.080 --> 00:57:38.500
is willing to pretend like none of that is happening and they're just friends while it's happening.

1399
00:57:39.160 --> 00:57:44.780
But for you to just look at her and say, hey, you were kind of unfaithful last night was

1400
00:57:44.780 --> 00:57:47.620
very shocking for her, and she had to shut that down.

1401
00:57:47.740 --> 00:57:48.680
She had to be like, I'm sorry.

1402
00:57:48.680 --> 00:57:50.100
I don't know what you're talking about.

1403
00:57:50.100 --> 00:57:53.700
You're just my friend, and we were hanging out after work.

1404
00:57:53.720 --> 00:57:57.100
So I don't know what you thought that was, but uncool.

1405
00:57:57.700 --> 00:57:58.060
Right.

1406
00:57:58.160 --> 00:58:03.160
That was her way of trying to get her boundary back and also just being defensive knowing

1407
00:58:03.160 --> 00:58:05.540
that she did something she shouldn't have, I think.

1408
00:58:05.540 --> 00:58:10.800
Well, I think whenever like there's a moment when Angela catches her with Pam Pong, then

1409
00:58:10.800 --> 00:58:13.120
Meredith catches the shirt coming up, right?

1410
00:58:13.360 --> 00:58:18.040
And then this moment when he calls it out, all of those moments are when Pam gets a mirror

1411
00:58:18.040 --> 00:58:24.240
held up to her behavior, and it makes her uncomfortable because she knows the right thing to do is say,

1412
00:58:24.360 --> 00:58:27.300
Roy, I'm in love with Jim, and we should break up.

1413
00:58:27.480 --> 00:58:27.620
Yeah.

1414
00:58:27.620 --> 00:58:32.060
But she's got all of these layers like you do in a relationship, and feelings probably of guilt

1415
00:58:32.060 --> 00:58:35.260
and obligation, and all of that all wrapped up into it.

1416
00:58:35.320 --> 00:58:37.040
So she doesn't know how to make that break.

1417
00:58:37.240 --> 00:58:37.500
Yeah.

1418
00:58:37.660 --> 00:58:41.840
And I think this is one of those moments where a mirror is held up, and she feels bad,

1419
00:58:41.920 --> 00:58:42.900
and she bristles at it.

1420
00:58:42.980 --> 00:58:48.080
And then it all ends with that final look between Michael and Jim, the little shrug.

1421
00:58:48.800 --> 00:58:49.680
Eh, women.

1422
00:58:49.960 --> 00:58:51.240
Ah, what are you going to do?

1423
00:58:51.380 --> 00:58:51.620
Yeah.

1424
00:58:52.920 --> 00:58:54.000
Two lonely guys.

1425
00:58:54.480 --> 00:58:56.200
Well, guys, that was the client.

1426
00:58:56.200 --> 00:58:57.400
That's the client.

1427
00:58:57.600 --> 00:59:02.260
Thank you so much, Melora Hardin and Tim Meadows for making this episode that much more special.

